#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:3
#: de7d1abcbf7c4fabb66402eb7f1f16ce
msgid "How to upgrade a Fedora template in-place"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:6
#: 4acea6bc196d4eaaad5838f0e40274b7
msgid "This page is intended for advanced users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:8
#: 98018ee8b8774463936b4599027225f0
msgid ""
"Most users will find it easier to doc:`install a fresh template <user/"
"templates/fedora/fedora:installing>` instead of upgrading in-place. If you "
"have made customizations or installed additional packages in the current "
"template that you want to preserve, then upgrading in-place may be the best "
"way to go."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:11
#: c5fb6efe062d4697a4875299aa8cc560
msgid ""
"This page provides instructions for performing an in-place upgrade of an "
"installed :doc:`Fedora Template </user/templates/fedora/fedora>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:14
#: 593e7f7fe2f0440281c311c9db8ee297
msgid ""
"In what follows the prompt on each line indicates where each command should "
"be entered: ``dom0``, ``fedora-<old>``, or ``fedora-<new>``, where ``<old>`` "
"is the fedora version number *from* which you are upgrading, and ``<new>`` "
"is the fedora version number *to* which you are upgrading. Remember to use "
"the right template *version*: eg clone ``fedora-<old>-minimal`` to ``fedora-"
"<new>-minimal``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:17
#: d3ef0e0877484fb5b5a8d9db70edad36
msgid "Summary instructions for standard Fedora templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:38
#: ead0518caafa49d4b71fc9ff0399c613
msgid "Detailed instructions for standard Fedora templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:41
#: d0d575aee05046aea7a6f71646ebd54b
msgid ""
"These instructions will show you how to upgrade the standard Fedora "
"template. The same general procedure may be used to upgrade any template "
"based on the standard Fedora template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:44
#: c7e498cba00e483685c40049a9c59a97
msgid "Ensure the existing template is not running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:51
#: b35585046b2f4005939fe16bcaf46879
msgid "Clone the existing template and start a terminal in the new template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:59
#: 8f0c7a0520e54052b7a8ffae38a652a2
msgid "Attempt the upgrade process in the new template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:68
#: 7ba6fa8e9ad24729ab5c52d1e95684b0
msgid ""
"**Note:** ``dnf`` might ask you to approve importing a new package signing "
"key. For example, you might see a prompt like this one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:80
#: 1b0d27d5191846c7ade28e9c5f2be670
msgid ""
"This key was already checked when it was installed (notice that the “From” "
"line refers to a location on your local disk), so you can safely say yes to "
"this prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:82
#: a0d7bf21b01b458ba0179d2391770cb0
msgid ""
"**Note:** If you encounter no errors, proceed to step 4. If you do encounter "
"errors, see the next two points first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:84
#: 2360954f5d4e4cd1bf7ff56caa773929
msgid ""
"If ``dnf`` reports that you do not have enough free disk space to proceed "
"with the upgrade process, create an empty file in dom0 to use as a cache and "
"attach it to the template as a virtual disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:92
#: a6f2469274a740bab9954da1d7658ede
msgid ""
"Then reattempt the upgrade process, but this time use the virtual disk as a "
"cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:102
#: e21581c9f445411184b74aa83dc43623
msgid "If this attempt is successful, proceed to step 4."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:104
#: 81af680fef6a4e64bb204b5c3fa41da5
msgid ""
"``dnf`` may error with the text: ``At least X MB more space needed on the / "
"filesystem.`` In this case, one option is to :doc:`resize the template’s "
"disk image </user/advanced-topics/resize-disk-image>` before reattempting "
"the upgrade process. (See :ref:`user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade:"
"additional information` below for other options.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:109
#: d4115b43cb9a4f9fba35ef4b60f250c4
msgid ""
"Check that you are on the correct (new) Fedora release. Do this check only "
"after completing the upgrade process. This is *not* a troubleshooting "
"procedure for fixing download issues from the repository. This check simply "
"verifies that your clone has successfully been upgraded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:117
#: 1491bb88b47f41a195cb99280f94f5aa
msgid ""
"(Optional) Trim the new template. (This should :ref:`no longer be necessary "
"<user/templates/templates:important notes>`, but it does not hurt. Some "
"users have `reported <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-issues/"
"issues/5055>`__ that it makes a difference.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:127
#: 3089fa8d3a7e4f87a40c7fa51993f0ef
msgid "Shut down the new template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:134
#: b34b501ac9534132ac30ee2b8c10c3b3
msgid "Remove the cache file, if you created one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:142
#: e5627b3eebba48a89c99d30f66e9c726
msgid "Set the template-name, which is used by the Qubes updater."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:149
#: ad1e477dddb14d6c9e33992b0422f816
msgid ""
"(Recommended) :ref:`Switch everything that was set to the old template to "
"the new template. <user/templates/templates:switching>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:151
#: b71231a8e30049c9a310c489a8f4b45c
msgid "(Optional) Make the new template the global default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:158
#: 3602424c25fd4dd5a085d9ce1c261177
msgid ""
"(Optional) :ref:`Uninstall the old template. <user/templates/templates:"
"uninstalling>` Make sure that the template you’re uninstalling is the old "
"one, not the new one!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:163
#: c0648471c71a4bf2af3b7ccb0b0db6af
msgid "Summary instructions for Fedora Minimal templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:166
#: c2760e9fe69844838919c1bc0bc8e1da
msgid ""
"**Note:** The prompt on each line indicates where each command should be "
"entered: ``dom0``, ``fedora-<old>``, or ``fedora-<new>``, where ``<old>`` is "
"the Fedora version number *from* which you are upgrading, and ``<new>`` is "
"the Fedora version number *to* which you are upgrading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:178
#: ca098f8870b24754840863bcdc2de2df
msgid "(Shut down template by any normal means.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:180
#: c9eb079691b84c17b3046c12ab204d54
msgid ""
"(If you encounter insufficient space issues, you may need to use the methods "
"described for the standard template above.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:183
#: 46e82045a85c4c098d815ab3c98f9b30
msgid "Standalones"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:186
#: 2ee8108b563f42ada8313f44f9c60d6c
msgid ""
"The procedure for upgrading a Fedora :doc:`standalone </user/advanced-topics/"
"standalones-and-hvms>` is the same as for a template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:189
#: 4845fba7f68d4c808739babf0dbcec32
msgid "Release-specific notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:192
#: b5b3ad971cad44bfb7a7529a32939adf
msgid ""
"See the `news <https://www.qubes-os.org/news/>`__ announcement for each "
"specific template release for any important notices about that particular "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:195
#: e2669e2e771741238fffa042f5c0625b
msgid "End-of-life (EOL) releases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:198
#: 171a7312700549f582bc6dff24d4a9b5
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend against using any Fedora release that has reached `end-"
"of-life (EOL) <https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/End_of_life>`__. Also see :doc:"
"`supported releases </user/downloading-installing-upgrading/supported-"
"releases>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:201
#: 1a49150ca1404d0ea321a5e10966b1e6
msgid "Additional information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:204
#: 57befa43b60d4d01b488e576de8ac95a
msgid "As mentioned above, you may encounter the following ``dnf`` error:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:212
#: fd3e1844187a4a2cac9908b983b18e93
msgid "In this case, you have several options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:214
#: 0c9dc2e75da043f889e5c1a71dfd3918
msgid ""
":doc:`Increase the template’s disk image size </user/advanced-topics/resize-"
"disk-image>`. This is the solution mentioned in the main instructions above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:216
#: 1de565e9c2ec4ad1a15bf9fef1b484fa
msgid ""
"Delete files in order to free up space. One way to do this is by "
"uninstalling packages. You may then reinstall them again after you finish "
"the upgrade process, if desired). However, you may end up having to increase "
"the disk image size anyway (see previous option)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:218
#: 3502819e991f452dbfb4a315a38d50f7
msgid ""
"Do the upgrade in parts, e.g., by using package groups. (First upgrade "
"``@core`` packages, then the rest.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/fedora/fedora-upgrade.rst:220
#: 58e00d4f88ba420c870708bd1fe04ddf
msgid ""
"Do not perform an in-place upgrade, see :ref:`Upgrading Fedora templates "
"<user/templates/fedora/fedora:upgrading>`."
msgstr ""
